It was not the best idea to run towards the armed policemen. You turned your head back, and longingly looked at the fence. No man can jump that high.
But when you heard gunshots, your body began to move instinctually by itself. You took hard off the ground and rocketed into the air, landing on the other side of the fence. No time to waste before your pursuers would find a roundabout way, you ran through the narrow streets up hill and down dale, trying to get as far from there as possible. 
Like a hairy whirlwind you ran into a side street and nearly bumped into a struggling couple. It appeared that another crime was in progress. A muscular skinny fellow wearing a mask and a leather jacket was quietly trying to snatch a bag from a woman. She was trying to fend him off. The sight of your appearance struck them like lightning. The woman's eyes bugged out, she immediately released her bag, and she ran behind the corner, screaming.  The mugger stepped back to the wall, brandishing the knife in his fist.